      "title": "tap-camelsrt: improve memory management",
      "message": "tap-camelsrt: improve memory management\n\nExpose the existing function `camelsrt_reset()` as the tap reset\nfunction. Add a `camelsrt_finish()` function for the tap finish\nfunction.\n\nRemove `filter` from the tap-state structure since it wasn't used for\nanything. (And it was leaked if `camelsrt_reset()` was called, since it\nnaively zeroes out the entire structure, including the pointer to the\nallocated filter string.) `register_tap_listener()` already takes a copy\nof the filter string so we don't need to allocate and track another\ncopy.\n\nReplace `0` with `TL_REQUIRES_NOTHING` in the call to\n`register_tap_listener()` to improve code self-documentation.\n",
      "author_name": "David Perry",
      "author_email": "boolean263@protonmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-04-15T10:33:40.000-04:00",
